Difficulty: medium. Complexity target: O(rows * cols) — each cell is enqueued and dequeued at most once time, O(rows * cols) for the BFS queue in the worst case space.

Probe test (pasted into the pad if they stall at hint level 3):
assert hours_to_freeze([[2, 1, 1, 1]]) == 3
(The most common wrong approach re-scans the grid each 'hour' while mutating it in place, so newly frozen cells spread again within the same left-to-right pass and the whole row cascades in one step, returning 1 instead of 3. Verified: reference returns 3, the in-place-scan naive returns 1.)

